    "skills": "add-fractions-with-unlike-denominators-ii",
    "question_text": "Add. $\\frac{1}{7} + \\frac{2}{3}$ ==_",
    "tag": "Gr6_17_E3",
    "question_number": "3_1",
    "question_type": "Fill in the blank",
    "correct_answers": [
      "13.0"
    ],
    "solution": [
      [
        "1/6",
        "To add the fractions, you can use the least common denominator. The least common denominator is the smallest whole number that is a multiple of both 7 and 3."
      ],
      [
        "2/6",
        "7 and 3 are prime numbers. You do not need to factor them. Multiply the prime numbers: $7 \\times 3 = 21$"
      ],
      [
        "3/6",
        "The least common denominator is 21. Find equivalent fractions with 21 as the denominator."
      ],
      [
        "4/6",
        "$\\frac{1 \\times 3}{7 \\times 3} = \\frac{3}{21}$ $\\frac{2 \\times 7}{3 \\times 7} = \\frac{14}{21}$"
      ],
      [
        "5/6",
        "Now add the fractions. Add the numerators and keep the denominators the same."
      ],
      [
        "6/6",
        "$\\frac{3}{21} + \\frac{14}{21} = \\frac{17}{21}$"
      ]
    ],
    "has_alternate_answers": false
  },
